{"tool_name":"modinterv","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"modinterv","home":"http://fisica.ufpr.br/modinterv","summary":"An automated online software for modeling epidemics.","addition_date":"2022-10-11T20:44:19.208243Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:27:12.492892Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"collections":["COVID-19"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:modinterv","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Ant\u00f4nio M.S. Mac\u00eado"},{"name":"Arthur A. Brum"},{"name":"Francisco A.G. Almeida"},{"name":"Gerson C. Duarte-Filho"},{"name":"Giovani L. Vasconcelos"},{"name":"Raydonal Ospina","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9884-9090","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"ModInterv","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.simpa.2022.100409","metadata":{"abstract":"The COVID-19 pandemic has proven the importance of mathematical tools to understand the evolution of epidemic outbreaks and provide reliable information to the general public and health authorities. In this perspective, we have developed ModInterv, an online software that applies growth models to monitor the evolution of the COVID-19 epidemic in locations chosen by the user among countries worldwide or states and cities in the USA or Brazil. This paper describes the software capabilities and its use both in recent research works and by technical committees assisting government authorities. Possible applications to other epidemics are also briefly discussed.","authors":[{"name":"Almeida F.A.G."},{"name":"Brum A.A."},{"name":"Duarte-Filho G.C."},{"name":"Macedo A.M.S."},{"name":"Ospina R."},{"name":"Vasconcelos G.L."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2022-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Software Impacts","title":"ModInterv: An automated onlin